WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.655 --> 00:00:19.076
next day Holmes was in a good mood when he showed up at my room before breakfast.

2
00:00:19.096 --> 00:00:23.139
"I've been awake since six o'clock and already put in two hours of work!"

3
00:00:23.559 --> 00:00:24.119
he announced.

4
00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:27.061
I finished tying my tie and put on my waistcoat.

5
00:00:27.761 --> 00:00:29.162
"I can tell that you've solved the case."

6
00:00:29.182 --> 00:00:31.723
"An excellent observation, my dear Watson.

7
00:00:32.123 --> 00:00:32.664
Look at this!"

8
00:00:33.472 --> 00:00:34.533
Holmes held out his hand.

9
00:00:35.174 --> 00:00:38.816
On his palm were three lumps of black clay speckled with something like sawdust.

10
00:00:38.836 --> 00:00:40.958
"You had only two lumps yesterday."

11
00:00:40.978 --> 00:00:45.582
"I added another one today, and I'm sure all three came from the same place."

12
00:00:46.362 --> 00:00:47.623
Holmes put the clay in his pocket.

13
00:00:47.643 --> 00:00:49.645
"Can you survive without breakfast?

14
00:00:50.446 --> 00:00:51.186
I'd like to go to St.

15
00:00:51.206 --> 00:00:53.348
Luke's College and put Soames out of his misery."

16
00:00:55.149 --> 00:00:58.932
When we arrived, Soames was so agitated that he could hardly stand still.

17
00:00:58.953 --> 00:01:00.454
"Thank goodness you're here!"

18
00:01:01.174 --> 00:01:02.976
Soames mopped his brow with a handkerchief.

19
00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:05.241
"Can the exam proceed as usual?"

20
00:01:05.261 --> 00:01:07.923
"Yes, go ahead," Holmes replied.

21
00:01:07.943 --> 00:01:10.445
"But what about the scoundrel who tried to cheat?"

22
00:01:11.085 --> 00:01:12.846
"Don't worry about him," Holmes said.

23
00:01:12.866 --> 00:01:16.429
"I know who he is, and he won't be competing for the scholarship.

24
00:01:16.989 --> 00:01:19.131
Now, let's arrange your chairs before we confront him."

25
00:01:19.771 --> 00:01:22.393
Holmes pulled three chairs into a row and took the middle one.

26
00:01:23.153 --> 00:01:27.436
Motioning for us to sit beside him, he glanced from side to side with a satisfied smile.

27
00:01:27.456 --> 00:01:31.539
"We look intimidating enough to strike fear into the heart of any guilty person.

28
00:01:32.812 --> 00:01:34.553
Soames, please ring the bell and summon your servant."

29
00:01:36.314 --> 00:01:39.516
When Bannister entered the room, he shrank back in surprise and fear.

30
00:01:39.536 --> 00:01:44.638
"Now, Bannister," Holmes said, "please tell us the truth about yesterday's incident."

31
00:01:45.319 --> 00:01:46.339
Bannister turned pale.

32
00:01:46.359 --> 00:01:48.660
"I've told you everything, sir."

33
00:01:48.680 --> 00:01:50.662
"Then let me make a suggestion.

34
00:01:51.162 --> 00:01:53.663
You pretended to be ill and sat down on the desk chair.

35
00:01:54.203 --> 00:01:58.386
Why? Because you wanted to conceal something that would identify whoever had been in the room."

36
00:01:58.406 --> 00:01:59.806
"Certainly not!"

37
00:02:00.367 --> 00:02:01.187
Bannister snapped.

38
00:02:01.747 --> 00:02:02.548
Holmes pressed on.

39
00:02:03.180 --> 00:02:03.920
"The moment Mr.

40
00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:06.981
Soames left the room, you released the person who was hiding in the bedroom."

41
00:02:07.001 --> 00:02:08.922
"There was no person, sir."

42
00:02:09.462 --> 00:02:10.682
Bannister looked defiant.

43
00:02:10.702 --> 00:02:13.903
"Ah, that's a pity because now I know that you've lied."

44
00:02:13.923 --> 00:02:17.244
"There was no person, sir," Bannister repeated.

45
00:02:18.024 --> 00:02:20.905
Holmes frowned as Bannister stubbornly refused to cooperate.

46
00:02:22.005 --> 00:02:24.106
Then he asked Soames to fetch Gilchrist.

47
00:02:24.866 --> 00:02:28.387
When they returned, the student looked cheerful—until he spotted Bannister.

48
00:02:28.407 --> 00:02:31.848
"Mr. Gilchrist, what led you to cheat on the exam?"

49
00:02:32.288 --> 00:02:32.928
Holmes asked.

50
00:02:33.524 --> 00:02:37.226
The horrified young man staggered and cast a reproachful look at Bannister.

51
00:02:37.246 --> 00:02:39.367
"I never said a word, Mr.

52
00:02:39.387 --> 00:02:41.148
Gilchrist!" Bannister protested.

53
00:02:41.168 --> 00:02:47.092
"But now, Bannister, you have said something incriminating, so I know you were involved," Holmes said.

54
00:02:47.112 --> 00:02:50.874
"As for you, young man, your only hope lies in a full confession."

55
00:02:51.514 --> 00:02:53.495
Gilchrist fell on his knees before Holmes.

56
00:02:54.076 --> 00:02:56.637
Burying his face in his hands, he burst into sobs.

57
00:02:56.657 --> 00:02:59.459
"We know you're not a hard-core criminal."

58
00:03:00.019 --> 00:03:01.640
Holmes patted him gently on the shoulder.

59
00:03:02.316 --> 00:03:04.337
"Perhaps it would be easier if I describe what happened.

60
00:03:04.917 --> 00:03:06.798
You can correct me if I get anything wrong."

61
00:03:08.479 --> 00:03:09.299
Gilchrist nodded.

62
00:03:09.319 --> 00:03:14.221
"When we were in the courtyard last evening," Holmes began, "I looked through Mr.

63
00:03:14.261 --> 00:03:14.921
Soames' window.

64
00:03:15.682 --> 00:03:18.563
I wondered how tall a man must be to see any papers on the desk.

65
00:03:19.303 --> 00:03:22.204
I'm six feet tall, and I could do it only by standing on my tiptoes.

66
00:03:23.085 --> 00:03:24.885
So the culprit had to be taller than I am."

67
00:03:25.706 --> 00:03:28.567
"I'm six feet, three inches," Gilchrist whispered.

68
00:03:28.587 --> 00:03:33.885
"Another clue was that you compete in the long jump, a track-and-field event that requires spiked shoes."

69
00:03:34.545 --> 00:03:35.586
Gilchrist nodded again.

70
00:03:36.326 --> 00:03:41.349
According to the great detective, Gilchrist had spent the afternoon on the athletic fields, practicing his jumps.

71
00:03:42.149 --> 00:03:44.490
He returned to the courtyard, carrying his jumping shoes.

72
00:03:45.110 --> 00:03:49.072
As he passed Soames' window, he saw some papers on the desk and wondered if they were the

73
00:03:49.132 --> 00:03:49.812
exam proofs.

74
00:03:52.053 --> 00:03:56.155
Gilchrist probably would have just continued on his way to his room, but then he noticed something.

75
00:03:56.775 --> 00:03:57.696
The key was in the door.

76
00:03:58.396 --> 00:04:02.459
"On a whim you decided to enter and see if the papers were indeed the proofs," Holmes said.

77
00:04:02.479 --> 00:04:04.540
"There was no risk involved at this point.

78
00:04:05.201 --> 00:04:08.643
If you got caught, you could simply say you'd popped in to ask a question.

79
00:04:09.243 --> 00:04:12.685
But when you realized you'd found the proofs, you couldn't resist the temptation.

80
00:04:13.306 --> 00:04:16.688
You put your shoes down on the desktop, but what did you drop on the desk chair?"

81
00:04:16.708 --> 00:04:19.230
"My gloves," Gilchrist said weakly.

82
00:04:19.250 --> 00:04:22.872
"Aha!" Holmes clapped, startling the poor student.

83
00:04:23.724 --> 00:04:27.065
"One at a time, you took the proofs to the table by the window, so that you could

84
00:04:27.085 --> 00:04:28.806
keep an eye out for Soames' return.

85
00:04:30.746 --> 00:04:34.707
When you heard him at the door, you grabbed your shoes, and the spikes cut the leather desktop.

86
00:04:35.307 --> 00:04:38.028
But as you ran for the bedroom, you forgot your gloves."

87
00:04:38.048 --> 00:04:43.830
"That explains the cut," I said, "but what do the black pieces of clay have to do with

88
00:04:43.910 --> 00:04:45.770
anything? And the sawdust?"

89
00:04:46.330 --> 00:04:47.951
Holmes removed the clay from his pocket.

90
00:04:48.631 --> 00:04:51.372
He had suspected that the clay had been clinging to the shoe spikes.

91
00:04:52.404 --> 00:04:56.606
So this morning he walked over to the athletic fields, where he discovered that black clay was used

92
00:04:56.646 --> 00:04:57.286
in the jump pit.

93
00:04:57.306 --> 00:05:01.828
"Sawdust is sprinkled over the clay to prevent the athletes from slipping."

94
00:05:02.408 --> 00:05:03.589
Holmes stared at the student.

95
00:05:03.609 --> 00:05:05.430
"Is my story correct, Mr.

96
00:05:05.450 --> 00:05:07.051
Gilchrist?" "Yes, sir."

97
00:05:07.811 --> 00:05:09.552
Gilchrist stood up and took a deep breath.

98
00:05:11.773 --> 00:05:12.973
Soames appeared to be shocked.

99
00:05:12.993 --> 00:05:15.014
"That's all you have to say, Mr.

100
00:05:15.054 --> 00:05:19.116
Gilchrist?" Gilchrist pulled a paper from his pocket and handed it to Soames.

101
00:05:20.092 --> 00:05:23.434
"I felt so guilty about cheating, I was up all night, writing you this letter.

102
00:05:24.454 --> 00:05:26.395
Read it and you'll see I'm withdrawing from the college."

103
00:05:27.235 --> 00:05:28.276
Soames looked surprised.

104
00:05:28.296 --> 00:05:30.897
"What made you change your mind about the scholarship?"

105
00:05:31.777 --> 00:05:33.098
Gilchrist pointed at Bannister.

106
00:05:33.118 --> 00:05:35.499
"This man persuaded me to do the right thing."

107
00:05:36.139 --> 00:05:38.360
Holmes turned to Bannister with a quizzical expression.

108
00:05:38.380 --> 00:05:40.841
"For many years I was a butler for Mr.

109
00:05:40.861 --> 00:05:42.642
Gilchrist's father," Bannister said.

110
00:05:42.662 --> 00:05:46.784
"When he died, I came here to work, but I never forgot my old employer.

111
00:05:47.600 --> 00:05:50.061
Out of loyalty to the father, I watched over the son."

112
00:05:51.921 --> 00:05:57.123
Bannister explained that when he came into the room yesterday, he noticed Gilchrist's gloves on the desk chair.

113
00:05:57.143 --> 00:05:59.483
"They're an unusual color, and if Mr.

114
00:05:59.543 --> 00:06:01.424
Soames saw them, he'd know they were Mr.

115
00:06:01.444 --> 00:06:06.925
Gilchrist's." So the faithful servant sat on the gloves and refused to budge until Soames went for Holmes.

116
00:06:07.645 --> 00:06:10.306
Then Gilchrist came out of the bedroom and confessed to Bannister.

117
00:06:10.326 --> 00:06:14.427
"It was my duty to speak to him as his father would have done," Bannister said.

118
00:06:14.447 --> 00:06:17.008
"I told him that he couldn't profit from cheating."

119
00:06:17.628 --> 00:06:18.288
"No, indeed."

120
00:06:18.989 --> 00:06:19.929
Holmes sprang to his feet.

121
00:06:20.549 --> 00:06:21.790
"I wish you good luck, young man.

122
00:06:22.410 --> 00:06:26.311
You may have fallen, but let's hope you learn from this experience and rise to new heights."

123
00:06:27.212 --> 00:06:27.812
He turned to me.

124
00:06:27.832 --> 00:06:31.353
"And now, Watson, I think we've earned some breakfast!"
